course: dictionary
lesson: 2343
title: Crusty, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which meaning is right. «Broken eczema skin can be infected by bacteria or the cold sore virus; crusty, weepy patches need a GP, and sudden painful blisters with fever need urgent help.» The words around crusty are skin, patches and weepy, so crusty describes skin with a hard, dry layer on it.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Crusty patches means patches with a hard, dry layer, and that makes sense. A hard, crisp outside would not fit the skin here, so the first meaning is the wrong one for this sentence.
explain: The same word works differently in other places. A crusty loaf has a hard, crisp outside, like fresh bread. A crusty old neighbour is grumpy and easily annoyed. Look at the words next to crusty each time, and they will show you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Crusty» means having a hard, crisp outside, like fresh bread.
fact: «Crusty» means covered with a hard, dry layer, like a crusty scab or crusty mud.
fact: A crusty person is grumpy and easily annoyed, and this is often an old person.
fact: Useful phrases: crusty bread, crusty roll and crusty old man.
exercise: Mum buys a crusty roll from the bakery. What does crusty mean here? | Soft and squashy all the way through | Cold and frozen | *A hard, crisp outside | Sweet and sugary
exercise: «Broken eczema skin ... crusty, weepy patches need a GP.» What does crusty mean in this sentence? | Smooth and shiny | *Covered with a hard, dry layer | Bright and colourful | Very hot to touch
exercise: Grandad is a crusty old man who grumbles at everyone. What does crusty suggest about him? | *Grumpy and easily annoyed | Very fast on his feet | Very kind and cuddly | Lost his glasses again
test: A doctor tells you a cut is crusty and starting to close up. What does crusty suggest? | *The cut is healing | The cut is covered in ice | The cut is full of sand | The cut is getting bigger
test: In a story, a crusty old neighbour is best described as | Full of happy songs | Hungry for bread | *Grumpy but may be kind inside | Tiny and very quiet
exam: Ella reads, «The dried mud on the boots was crusty.» What does crusty mean? | Soft and wet | Very cold | *Covered with a hard, dry layer | Shiny like glass
